  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bhim Singh vs State And N.S.A. on 20 September, 2019 Author: Sudhir Agarwal Bench: Sudhir Agarwal High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 34 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 596 of 1990 Revisionist :- Bhim Singh Opposite Party :- State And N.S.A. Counsel for Revisionist :- V.K. Sharma,Vinod Kumar Shukla",
    "facts": "It is contended by learned counsel for Revisionist that when Food Inspector was taking sample, it was mentioned by Revisionist that he is selling mixed milk of cow and buffalo but that has been ignored and the sample has been taken as that of buffalo's milk and same has been chemically examined accordingly. Therefore, entire prosecution case falls for the reason that sample was taken of mixed milk of buffalo and cow, hence the ratio of buffalo's milk could not have been assessed. Learned counsel for Revisionist further submitted that in this regard a defence witness was also examined.",
